{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>A scoffer seeks wisdom</b> — to teach wisdom." "<b>and there is none</b> — because he is occupied with mockery, he cannot know it." "<b>and knowledge to the discerning</b> — to a discerning man it is easy to learn. He will remember, as in (Proverbs 24:14): \"and knowledge to your soul will be pleasant.\""], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:41.828055042Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}